  "method": [
    {
      "text": "Real-session gold was labeled by hand, call by call. Scenario gold comes from each scenario's expectations, written before its runs; calls no expectation could settle were labeled by hand in review.",
      "see": [
        "TAXONOMY.md",
        "docs/scenarios-design.md"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A label is scored only where the taxonomy asks it, so n differs by label. A labeler's answer is its most probable one (0.5 for yes/no labels). Calls a labeler didn't label, such as calls the hosted labeler's secret screen refused, are listed as not labeled, not counted as errors.",
      "see": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Accuracy carries a 95% Wilson score interval. Scenario runs repeat the same calls, so accuracy per shape counts each unique call shape (the tool plus its normalized arguments) once, as the share of its calls answered correctly, and averages over shapes.",
      "see": []
    },
    {
      "text": "ECE (expected calibration error, 10 equal-width bins) compares the probability of each answer with whether it was right. At these sizes it is only indicative.",
      "see": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Labels set by rule are written by code from facts the parser already knows, without asking a labeler. They are listed apart and not counted in either labeler's accuracy.",
      "see": [
        "TAXONOMY.md"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Claude Code's telemetry doesn't capture everything the agent sees, and the labelers have known weaknesses that v0 ships with.",
      "see": [
        "docs/findings/capture-gaps.md",
        "docs/findings/known-limitations.md"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
